   "source": [
    "# RBI Policy Tone Analyzer (NLP with FinBERT)\n",
    "**What it does:** Reads one or two central bank documents (PDF), scores every sentence as positive, negative or neutral using **FinBERT** (an AI model trained on financial text), and shows the overall tone, the most positive and most negative sentences, and how the tone changed between two documents.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why it matters:** Markets and analysts read the *tone* of RBI statements, not just the numbers. This project turns text into measurable data.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tech:** Python, Hugging Face Transformers (FinBERT), PyTorch, Pandas, Matplotlib, Google Colab\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run:** Open in Google Colab and run each step in order. Upload 1 or 2 PDFs when asked. For a comparison, upload two RBI Monetary Policy Statements, e.g. August 2026 and October 2026."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8efa7d52",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Install libraries"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "df3223c6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q pypdf transformers torch pandas matplotlib"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "71f180cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Upload your PDF(s)\n",
    "Select one PDF, or hold Ctrl and select two to compare them."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8f17479e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "uploaded = files.upload()\n",
    "pdf_names = list(uploaded.keys())\n",
    "print('Loaded:', pdf_names)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dba8a9d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Read the PDFs and split them into sentences\n",
    "The model scores one sentence at a time, so we first clean the text and split it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f5c0305f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import re\n",
    "from pypdf import PdfReader\n",
    "\n",
    "def read_sentences(path, min_len=40, max_len=400, limit=250):\n",
    "    text = ' '.join((p.extract_text() or '') for p in PdfReader(path).pages)\n",
    "    text = ' '.join(text.split())\n",
    "    parts = re.split(r'(?<=[.!?])\\s+(?=[A-Z])', text)\n",
    "    return [s for s in parts if min_len <= len(s) <= max_len][:limit]\n",
    "\n",
    "docs = {name: read_sentences(name) for name in pdf_names}\n",
    "for name, sents in docs.items():\n",
    "    print(name, '->', len(sents), 'sentences')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5e54d8b3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Load the FinBERT model\n",
    "This downloads the model the first time (about 400 MB), so it can take a few minutes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c682a0e2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "from transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSequenceClassification\n",
    "\n",
    "model_name = 'ProsusAI/finbert'\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\n",
    "model = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(model_name)\n",
    "model.eval()\n",
    "\n",
    "labels = {int(i): l.lower() for i, l in model.config.id2label.items()}\n",
    "pos_idx = [i for i, l in labels.items() if l == 'positive'][0]\n",
    "neg_idx = [i for i, l in labels.items() if l == 'negative'][0]\n",
    "print('Labels:', labels)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "20f15de3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Score every sentence\n",
    "For each sentence the model gives probabilities for positive, negative and neutral. We keep the top label and also compute a **tone score** = P(positive) - P(negative). The score runs from -1 (very negative) to +1 (very positive)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3899d48c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "def classify(sentences, batch_size=16):\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for i in range(0, len(sentences), batch_size):\n",
    "        batch = sentences[i:i + batch_size]\n",
    "        enc = tokenizer(batch, return_tensors='pt', padding=True, truncation=True, max_length=128)\n",
    "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "            probs = torch.softmax(model(**enc).logits, dim=-1)\n",
    "        for sent, p in zip(batch, probs):\n",
    "            top = int(p.argmax())\n",
    "            rows.append({'sentence': sent,\n",
    "                         'label': labels[top],\n",
    "                         'confidence': float(p[top]),\n",
    "                         'score': float(p[pos_idx] - p[neg_idx])})\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "results = {name: classify(sents) for name, sents in docs.items()}\n",
    "for name, df in results.items():\n",
    "    print(name)\n",
    "    print(df['label'].value_counts().to_string(), '\\n')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3b38c276",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Overall tone"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0295a1d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    name: {\n",
    "        'Sentences': len(df),\n",
    "        'Positive %': round((df.label == 'positive').mean() * 100, 1),\n",
    "        'Negative %': round((df.label == 'negative').mean() * 100, 1),\n",
    "        'Neutral %': round((df.label == 'neutral').mean() * 100, 1),\n",
    "        'Tone score (avg)': round(df.score.mean(), 3),\n",
    "    } for name, df in results.items()\n",
    "}).T\n",
    "summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6544f7a5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7: Charts"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3cc2f327",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
    "share = pd.DataFrame({n: df.label.value_counts(normalize=True) * 100 for n, df in results.items()}).T\n",
    "share = share.reindex(columns=['positive', 'neutral', 'negative']).fillna(0)\n",
    "share.plot(kind='bar', ax=ax[0], color=['#2e8b57', '#9aa0a6', '#c0392b'], title='Share of sentences by tone (%)')\n",
    "ax[0].set_xticklabels([n[:18] for n in share.index], rotation=20)\n",
    "\n",
    "tone = summary['Tone score (avg)']\n",
    "tone.plot(kind='bar', ax=ax[1], color='#3B3F8F', title='Average tone score')\n",
    "ax[1].axhline(0, color='black', linewidth=0.8)\n",
    "ax[1].set_xticklabels([n[:18] for n in tone.index], rotation=20)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "319a60d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 8: Read the most negative and most positive sentences\n",
    "Always read the actual sentences. The AI is a helper, not the final judge."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3fe6fe2a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for name, df in results.items():\n",
    "    print('=' * 80)\n",
    "    print(name)\n",
    "    print('\\nMOST NEGATIVE:')\n",
    "    for _, r in df.nsmallest(3, 'score').iterrows():\n",
    "        print(f\"  ({r.score:+.2f}) {r.sentence[:220]}\")\n",
    "    print('\\nMOST POSITIVE:')\n",
    "    for _, r in df.nlargest(3, 'score').iterrows():\n",
    "        print(f\"  ({r.score:+.2f}) {r.sentence[:220]}\")"
   ]
  },
